<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sack of Surat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1664">1664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-maratha-wars">Mughal–Maratha Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surat">Surat</a> in 1664 was a raid by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> on the wealthy Mughal port city of Surat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. His forces seized large amounts of wealth from the city over several days. Accounts of the Maratha Empire cite the raid as an example of Maratha logistical skill and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psychological-warfare">psychological warfare</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sack-of-surat.jpg" alt="Sack of Surat" width="286" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sack_of_Surat_by_Shivaji.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
